<newsitem itemid="531474" id="root" date="1997-04-23" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ERPM posts Q1 pre-capex net loss.</title>
<headline>ERPM posts Q1 pre-capex net loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit/(loss) before</p>
<p>    capital spending		   11.14 loss vs 18.68 profit</p>
<p>    Capital spending		    6.69	vs  8.71</p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    - underground ERPM			1,415 vs 1,892</p>
<p>    - surface ERPM				321 vs 316</p>
<p>    - surface Benoni			    361 vs 404</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    - underground ERPM		    258,000 vs 296,000</p>
<p>    - surface ERPM			  530,000 vs 562,000</p>
<p>    - surface Benoni			293,000 vs 394,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    - underground ERPM			 5.48 vs 6.39</p>
<p>    - surface ERPM			     0.61 vs 0.56</p>
<p>    - surface Benoni			   1.23 vs 1.03</p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - underground ERPM		     59,059 vs 52,110</p>
<p>    - surface ERPM			   31,249 vs 33,075</p>
<p>    - surface Benoni			 50,590 vs 54,518</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - underground, surface ERPM	  50,966 vs 56,152</p>
<p>    - surface Benoni			 52,064 vs 56,145</p>
<p>Full name: East Rand Proprietary Mines Ltd, managed by Randgold and Exploration Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The decrease in tonnage was the result of the closure of L-Shaft which, together with the implementation of a rationalisation programme, resulted in reduced working cost levels.</p>
<p>A decrease in yield was experienced at the Far East Vertical Shaft, which contributes 57 percent to the total underground production. The rationalisation strategy is ongoing and is accompanied by an increase in production from the Far East Vertical Shaft.</p>
<p>Surface operations were adversely affected by heavy rains. In addition, the production levels at Benoni section continued to be affected by remedial work on the milling action.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
